Chat Service API
A production-ready Chat Session & Message Management REST API built with Spring Boot 3.3.5, MySQL 8, and Redis 7.

Quick Start with Docker
The fastest way to run the entire application — one command starts everything.

Step 1 — Clone the Repository
git clone https://github.com/nasreenazamkhan/chat-service.git
cd chat-service

Step 2 — Create Environment File
cp .env.example .env

Step 3 — Start All Services
docker compose up --build

Step 4 — Verify Everything Is Running
docker compose ps

Step 5 — Open Swagger UI
http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui/index.html


API Documentation Swagger
The API is fully documented and interactive via Swagger UI.
Swagger UI
http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui/index.html


How to Authenticate in Swagger UI

Open http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui/index.html
Click the  Authorize button (top right)
Enter:
X-API-KEY → my-local-dev-api-key-12345
X-User-Id → user-001

Click Authorize then Close
All Try it out requests now include your credentials automatically